From: conda-forge fastplotlib-feedstock
Subject: [PATCH] Loosen the exact pygfx pin to a lower bound

fastplotlib pins ``pygfx==0.17.0`` exactly:
https://github.com/fastplotlib/fastplotlib/blob/v0.7.0/pyproject.toml#L23

conda-forge ships a single pygfx build per channel state and resolves the
compatible version through the solver, so the exact pin only serves to make
``pip check`` fail whenever the installed pygfx moves past 0.17.0.  Relax it
to ``>=0.17.0``, matching the ``run`` requirement expressed in meta.yaml.

Not applicable upstream as-is: upstream deliberately pins exactly.
---
diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 77d4c55..5ac51d1 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ keywords = [
 requires-python = ">= 3.11"
 dependencies = [
     "numpy>=2.1.0",
-    "pygfx==0.17.0",
+    "pygfx>=0.17.0",
     "wgpu",          # Let pygfx constrain the wgpu version
     "cmap>=0.1.3",
     # (this comment keeps this list multiline in VSCode)
